From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: a click on another display keeps the pointer and keys

What: the main window's windowDidResignKey: no longer lets go of the
pointer and the keyboard when the resign comes from a click in a head
window (the window of another display) that its mouseDown: hands straight
back (handKeyBack's rule: the main window on screen, its Space shown, QEMU
in front; ui/omacvm-key-handback.h). On the next turn of the main loop the
main window must be key again; if it is not, the let-go runs then. Every
other resign lets go as before: the escape combo and swipes (no click, the
main window's Space not shown), Command-Tab and other apps, Mission
Control, a hidden main window. handKeyBack uses the same rule.
OMACVM_POINTER_DEBUG=1 logs "omacvm-pointer: key to another display's
window at a click: pointer and keys kept".

Why: every click on an external display's VM window let go of the pointer
and took it again (#563): ungrabMouse showed the Mac's cursor and the
click's grab hid it again, the full-screen guard let go of its hold (a
warp of the Mac's cursor, which #561 makes up for), and raiseAllKeys
released held keys in the guest (a Shift-click there arrived as a plain
click: only a key going down presses a modifier again). The key comes back
within the same event, so nothing needs letting go.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's omacvm-cocoa-displays.patch).
Test: Tests/display/test-key-handback.sh (the rules; with ui/cocoa.m the
wiring, --self-test: the wiring checks fail on the code before) at build
time and in CI. Applies after omacvm-cocoa-head-key-same-space.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -2209,6 +2209,58 @@ - (void) omacvmHeadEvent:(NSEvent *)event view:(NSView *)view output:(int)output
 }
 @end
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM (#563): a click in another display's window (a head window) makes
+ * it key for a moment, and its mouseDown: hands the key straight back
+ * (handKeyBack). The main window keeps the pointer and the keyboard across
+ * that: no let-go of the grab and the full-screen guard (the Mac's cursor
+ * was shown and hidden again at every click, with a warp), no held key
+ * released in the guest. ui/omacvm-key-handback.h decides. Main thread.
+ */
+#include "ui/omacvm-key-handback.h"
+
+static OmacVMHandback omacvm_handback;
+
+/* The main window stopped being key: let go of the pointer and the keyboard. */
+static void omacvm_key_let_go(void)
+{
+    omacvm_pointer_left(&omacvm_ptr);
+    [cocoaView ungrabMouse];
+    [cocoaView raiseAllKeys];
+}
+
+/* The main window resigned key: a click's hand-back (keep everything)? */
+static bool omacvm_resign_kept(void)
+{
+    NSWindow *main = [cocoaView window];
+    NSEvent *e = [NSApp currentEvent];
+    NSEventType t = e ? [e type] : (NSEventType)0;
+    OmacVMResignIn in = {
+        .click = t == NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown || t == NSEventTypeRightMouseDown ||
+                 t == NSEventTypeOtherMouseDown,
+        .in_head = e && [e window] != main && omacvm_is_our_window([e window]),
+        .main_visible = [main isVisible],
+        .main_space = [main isOnActiveSpace],
+        .active = [NSApp isActive],
+    };
+
+    if (!omacvm_handback_keep(&omacvm_handback, &in)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (omacvm_pointer_debug) {
+        info_report("omacvm-pointer: key to another display's window at a click: pointer and keys kept");
+    }
+    /* After the click's mouseDown: (same event) the key is back; if not, let go now. */
+    dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+        if (omacvm_handback_settle(&omacvm_handback, [[cocoaView window] isKeyWindow])) {
+            if (omacvm_pointer_debug) {
+                info_report("omacvm-pointer: the key did not come back from the click: let go");
+            }
+            omacvm_key_let_go();
+        }
+    });
+    return true;
+}
 
 
 /*
@@ -2571,9 +2623,11 @@ - (NSApplicationPresentationOptions) window:(NSWindow *)window
 - (void) windowDidResignKey: (NSNotification *)aNotification
 {
     COCOA_DEBUG("%s\n", __func__);
-    omacvm_pointer_left(&omacvm_ptr);
-    [cocoaView ungrabMouse];
-    [cocoaView raiseAllKeys];
+    /* OmacVM: not at a click in another display's window (the key comes straight back). */
+    if (omacvm_resign_kept()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    omacvm_key_let_go();
 }
 
 /*
@@ -6555,11 +6609,14 @@ - (void)otherMouseDragged:(NSEvent *)e { [self send:e button:-1 down:false]; }
  * combo or a swipe moves the main window's display to another Space, and
  * making the main window key then switched that display straight back).
  * Only while the main window's Space shows. The click still goes to the VM.
+ * The main window kept the pointer and the keys meanwhile: its resign at
+ * this click used the same rule (omacvm_resign_kept, #563).
  */
 - (void)handKeyBack
 {
     NSWindow *main = [cocoaView window];
-    if ([main isVisible] && [main isOnActiveSpace] && [NSApp isActive] && ![main isKeyWindow]) {
+    if (omacvm_handback_ok([main isVisible], [main isOnActiveSpace], [NSApp isActive],
+                           [main isKeyWindow])) {
         [main makeKeyWindow];
     }
 }
